    }
  ],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Suppose we find an original zero at row 3, column 3.",
      "start_ms": 0,
      "end_ms": 4320,
      "start_frame": 0,
      "end_frame": 130,
      "word_count": 11
    },
    {
      "text": "Do we really need to remember every number in the original matrix?",
      "start_ms": 5000,
      "end_ms": 9620,
      "start_frame": 150,
      "end_frame": 289,
      "word_count": 12
    },
    {
      "text": "No.",
      "start_ms": 10400,
      "end_ms": 10820,
      "start_frame": 312,
      "end_frame": 325,
      "word_count": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "For the final answer, we only need two facts, which rows contained a zero, and which columns contained a zero.",
      "start_ms": 11800,
      "end_ms": 19400,
      "start_frame": 354,
      "end_frame": 582,
      "word_count": 20
    },
    {
      "text": "That is much less information.",
      "start_ms": 19980,
      "end_ms": 21820,
      "start_frame": 599,
      "end_frame": 655,
      "word_count": 5
    },
    {
      "text": "Instead of copying the whole matrix, we can keep one marker for every row, and one marker for every column.",
      "start_ms": 22520,
      "end_ms": 30440,
      "start_frame": 676,
      "end_frame": 913,
      "word_count": 20
    },
    {
      "text": "If row 3 contains an original zero, mark row 3.",
      "start_ms": 31240,
      "end_ms": 35140,
      "start_frame": 937,
      "end_frame": 1054,
      "word_count": 10
    },
    {
      "text": "If column 3 contains an original zero, mark column 3.",
      "start_ms": 35800,
      "end_ms": 40400,
      "start_frame": 1074,
      "end_frame": 1212,
      "word_count": 10
    },
    {
      "text": "Then after discovery is finished, those markers tell us exactly where zeros must go.",
      "start_ms": 40740,
      "end_ms": 46980,
      "start_frame": 1222,
      "end_frame": 1409,
      "word_count": 14
    },
    {
